      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "From my experience applying cloth component to my avatar, the bug of \"fly into the air\" still exists. As far as I know, at least in Unity3d 5.6, any cloth will not apply forces to the environment. For VRChat, I think it might be avatars being pushed up by colliding with the cloth mesh that caused this bug. I'm looking forward to any response from the developers and hope this could be fixed very soon.\nUpdated: I found out that it is my own fault causing this problem. Set the colliders to trigger solves this problem.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
