  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Cloth physics would be so much better using the builtin Unity Cloth component with meshes, but VRChat spawns characters and interacts with physics meshes in a way that causes the character to fly in directions for no reason when running, and the cloth mesh becomes clipped and locked outside of standard parameters. Once it does this and you move in the Y direction in any form while running, you spaz out and fly into the air. I think the cloth mesh is interacting with the environment and causing acceleration on the character? As well as character spawns causing acceleration against the cloth. Please fix this as Dynamic bones has limits and the only other whitelisted physics possibilities are Cloth and Rigidbody (the latter of which is extremely hard to set up)",
